# Baseline security headers for every page (Netlify serves this from the publish dir).
# Added 2026-08-21 from the security scan (M2). Intentionally conservative:
#  - X-Frame-Options DENY: the marketing site is never framed by us; blocks
#    clickjacking. (This governs OTHERS framing us; it does NOT stop us embedding
#    the Cloudflare Turnstile iframe, which is us->them.)
#  - HSTS has NO includeSubDomains / preload on purpose: oscen.ai has live
#    subdomains (crm/demo/dashboard) and preload is hard to undo. Apex/www only.
#  - No Content-Security-Policy yet: the site loads Meta Pixel / GTM / Plausible /
#    Google Fonts / three.js, so a CSP needs a Report-Only rollout first (tracked
#    in PROGRESS.md, M2 follow-up). These headers do not touch script loading.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
